WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.883
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 0: Alphabet & Sounds.

2
00:00:03.963 --> 00:00:12.322
You will meet all the letters of the alphabet — big letters
and small letters — and learn the sound each one makes.

3
00:00:12.402 --> 00:00:19.881
You will trace letters, say their sounds, and blend
them into your first little words like cat and sun.

4
00:00:19.961 --> 00:00:24.798
You will also learn your first
sight words and read tiny sentences.

5
00:00:24.878 --> 00:00:30.008
Take your time: knowing your letters
well matters more than going fast.

6
00:00:30.088 --> 00:00:36.173
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

7
00:00:36.253 --> 00:00:43.339
By the end of this unit, you will be able to
recognise and name uppercase and lowercase letters.

8
00:00:43.419 --> 00:00:48.117
You will also connect letters
a-z with their most common sounds.

9
00:00:48.197 --> 00:00:52.745
You will also hear and say beginning sounds in familiar words.

10
00:00:52.825 --> 00:00:55.507
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

11
00:00:55.587 --> 00:01:01.876
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: apple, ball, cat, dog, elephant, fish.

12
00:01:01.956 --> 00:01:08.397
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

13
00:01:08.477 --> 00:01:16.054
The reading sequence includes Week 1: Learn the
Alphabet (A–Z) and Week 2: Phonics (Letter Sounds a–m).

14
00:01:16.134 --> 00:01:21.258
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

15
00:01:21.338 --> 00:01:25.718
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

16
00:01:25.798 --> 00:01:29.488
The first language focus is The letter A says aaa.

17
00:01:29.568 --> 00:01:32.429
Say the aaa sound, not the letter name.

18
00:01:32.509 --> 00:01:36.123
Open your mouth wide, like Sami saying a-a-apple.

19
00:01:36.203 --> 00:01:41.024
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

20
00:01:41.104 --> 00:01:44.640
In speaking, you will complete Sound and say 1.

21
00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:48.485
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

22
00:01:48.565 --> 00:01:56.331
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

23
00:01:56.411 --> 00:01:58.108
You are ready to begin.

24
00:01:58.188 --> 00:02:05.601
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

25
00:02:05.681 --> 00:02:13.249
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
